  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Leadership and Governance in African Women?s Rights Organisations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Across Africa women continue to face discrimination, marginalization and inequalities manifest in forms of gender based violence, high rates of maternal and infant mortality; poor access to healthcare; and women bearing a disproportionate burden of care as a result of chronic poverty. Weak leadership and governance structures have been identified as key factors in the persistence of these challenges. AWDF will introduce an innovative, long-term and participatory approach to strengthening leadership at the individual and organisational levels. This way, women and their organisations can secure and protect their rights, enhance access to services, and have a voice to represent their interests.</narrative>
  </description>
